Problem:
Evaluate $(1+2i)6-3i$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to expand the expression:

\begin{align*}
(1+2i)(6-3i) &= 1\cdot6 + 1(-3i) + 2i\cdot6 + 2i\cdot(-3i) \\
&= 6 - 3i + 12i - 6i^2 \\
&= 6 - 3i + 12i + 6 \\
&= 12 + 9i.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{12+9i}$.
