Problem:
Simplify $(3-i)(6+2i)$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to expand the expression:

{align*}
(3-i)(6+2i) &= 3(6) + 3(2i) - i(6) - i(2i) \\
&= 18 + 6i - 6i - 2i^2 \\
&= 18 + 0i - 2(-1) \\
&= 18 + 2 \\
&= \boxed{20}.
{align*}
