Problem:
Evaluate $\sqrt[3]{12}\times \sqrt[3]{20}\times \sqrt[3]{15}\times \sqrt[3]{60}$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the property of cube roots that states $\sqrt[3]{a} \times \sqrt[3]{b} = \sqrt[3]{ab}$. Applying this property, we have:

$$\sqrt[3]{12} \times \sqrt[3]{20} \times \sqrt[3]{15} \times \sqrt[3]{60} = \sqrt[3]{12 \times 20 \times 15 \times 60}$$

Now, we calculate the product inside the cube root:

$$12 \times 20 \times 15 \times 60 = 216000$$

Next, we take the cube root of 216000:

$$\sqrt[3]{216000} = 60$$

Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{60}$.
====================

