Problem:
Simplify $(5-3i)(-4+3i)$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to simplify the expression:

{align*}
(5-3i)(-4+3i) &= 5(-4) + 5(3i) - 3i(-4) + 3i(3i) \\
&= -20 + 15i + 12i + 9i^2 \\
&= -20 + 27i - 9 \\
&= -29 + 27i.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the simplified expression is $\boxed{-29 + 27i}$.
