Problem:
Solve the inequality $$-13(r+5) + 25 > 4(r-10)$$for $r$. Express your answer in interval notation.

Solution:
answer:  First, simplify the inequality:

$$-13(r+5) + 25 > 4(r-10)$$

$$-13r - 65 + 25 > 4r - 40$$

$$-13r - 40 > 4r - 40$$

$$-13r - 4r > -40 + 40$$

$$-17r > 0$$

$$r < 0$$

Therefore, the solution to the inequality is $\boxed{(-\infty, 0)}$.
====================

