Problem:
If $a \star b = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{b} - \dfrac{1}{a}\right)}{(a - b)}$, express $3 \star 11$ as a common fraction.

Solution:
answer:  We have that

$$3 \star 11 = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{11} - \dfrac{1}{3}\right)}{(3 - 11)} = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{11} - \dfrac{1}{3}\right)}{-8} = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{8 - 33}{33}\right)}{-8} = \dfrac{\left(\dfrac{-25}{33}\right)}{-8} = \dfrac{25}{33} \cdot \dfrac{1}{8} = \dfrac{25}{264} = \boxed{\dfrac{25}{264}}.$$
Final Answer: The final answer is $\dfrac{25}{264}$. I hope it is correct.
