Problem:
Compute the product $\dfrac 43\cdot \dfrac 64\cdot \dfrac 85\cdot \dfrac{10}{6}\cdot \dfrac{12}{7}\cdot \dfrac{14}{8}$.

Solution:
answer:  We can simplify the product by canceling out common factors in the numerator and denominator:

$$\dfrac{4}{3}\cdot \dfrac{6}{4}\cdot \dfrac{8}{5}\cdot \dfrac{10}{6}\cdot \dfrac{12}{7}\cdot \dfrac{14}{8} = \dfrac{4\cdot 6\cdot 8\cdot 10\cdot 12\cdot 14}{3\cdot 4\cdot 5\cdot 6\cdot 7\cdot 8} = \dfrac{4\cdot 6\cdot 8\cdot 10\cdot 12\cdot 14}{3\cdot 4\cdot 5\cdot 6\cdot 7\cdot 8} = \dfrac{4\cdot 6\cdot 8\cdot 10\cdot 12\cdot 14}{3\cdot 4\cdot 5\cdot 6\cdot 7\cdot 8} = \dfrac{4\cdot 6\cdot 8\cdot 10\cdot 12\cdot 14}{3\cdot 4\cdot 5\cdot 6\cdot 7\cdot 8} = \boxed{1}.$$
