Problem:
A TV screen measures 24 by 16 inches. If each dimension is increased by 20$\%$, by what percent is the area increased?

Solution:
answer:  The original area of the TV screen is $24 \times 16 = 384$ square inches.

If each dimension is increased by 20%, the new dimensions will be $24 \times 1.2 = 29$ inches and $16 \times 1.2 = 19.2$ inches.

The new area of the TV screen is $29 \times 19.2 = 556.8$ square inches.

The increase in area is $556.8 - 384 = 172.8$ square inches.

The percentage increase in area is $\left(\frac{172.8}{384}\right) \times 100 \approx 44.44\%$.

Therefore, the area is increased by approximately $\boxed{44.44\%}$.
====================

