Problem:
The operation @ is defined as $\frac{m}{n}@\frac{p}{q} = (m)(p)\left(\frac{q}{n}\right)$ for simplified fractions $\frac{p}{q}$.  What is the simplified value of $\frac{7}{30}@\frac{10}{21}$?

Solution:
answer:  We have that $\frac{7}{30}@\frac{10}{21} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{21}{30} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \frac{7}{30}\cdot\frac{10}{21}\cdot\frac{7}{10} = \boxed{1}$.
====================

