Problem:
Let $f(x) = x - \lfloor \sqrt{x} \rfloor^2$. What is $f(101) + f(102) + f(103) + \cdots + f(110)$?

Solution:
answer:  We have that $f(x) = x - \lfloor \sqrt{x} \rfloor^2$. For $x \in [101, 110]$, $\lfloor \sqrt{x} \rfloor = 10$, so $f(x) = x - 10^2 = x - 100$. Therefore,

$$f(101) + f(102) + f(103) + \cdots + f(110) = (101 - 100) + (102 - 100) + \cdots + (110 - 100) + (101 - 100) = 1 + 2 + \cdots + 10 = \boxed{55}.$$
