Problem:
In the graph below, each grid line counts as one unit. The line shown below passes through the point $(1001,n)$ (not shown on graph).  Find $n$.
[asy]size(250,0);
add(shift(-10,-10)*grid(20,20));
draw((-10,0)--(10,0),linewidth(2));
draw((0,-10)--(0,10),linewidth(2));
label("x",(10,0),E);
label("y",(0,10),N);
draw((-10,-2.71) -- (10,8.71),blue,Arrows);[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  The slope of the line is $\frac{8.71 - (-2.71)}{10 - (-10)} = \frac{11.42}{20} = 0.571$. Therefore, the equation of the line is $y = 0.571x - 2.71$. Substituting $x = 1001$ into the equation, we get $y = 0.571(1001) - 2.71 = 571.571 - 2.71 = 568.861$. Therefore, $n = \boxed{568.861}$.
====================

