Problem:
Find the product of all real values of $y$ such that  $|{-2y}|\cdot\left|{-\dfrac{y}{2}}\right| = 36$.

Solution:
answer:  We have that $|{-2y}|\cdot\left|{-\dfrac{y}{2}}\right| = |2y|\cdot|\frac{y}{2}| = |y^2| = 36$. Therefore, $y^2 = 36$ or $y^2 = -36$. Solving these equations, we get $y = 6$ or $y = -6$. The product of all real values of $y$ is $6\cdot(-6) = \boxed{-36}$.
