answer:  Since $a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots$ is an arithmetic progression with common difference $1$, we have $a_2+a_4+a_6+a_8+\dots+a_{98}=a_1+a_2+a_3+\dots+a_{98}=\boxed{137}$.
