Problem:
You have a square that has a side length of $1$ centimeter. Each minute, $2$ centimeters are added to the side length. After $10$ minutes, what will be the difference between the area of the last square and the area of the initial square in square centimeters (do not include the units in your answer)?

Solution:
answer:  The initial area of the square is $1^2 = 1$ square centimeters.

After 10 minutes, the side length of the square will be $1 + 2 \times 10 = 21$ centimeters.

The area of the square after 10 minutes is $21^2 = 441$ square centimeters.

The difference between the area of the last square and the area of the initial square is $441 - 1 = 440$ square centimeters.

Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{440}$.
