Problem:
Find the sum of the coefficients in the polynomial $3(x^{10} - x^7 + 2x^3 - x + 7) + 4(x^3 - 2x^2 - 5)$ when it is simplified.

Solution:
answer:  First, distribute the constants inside the parentheses:

$$3(x^{10} - x^7 + 2x^3 - x + 7) + 4(x^3 - 2x^2 - 5) = 3x^{10} - 3x^7 + 6x^3 - 3x + 21 + 4x^3 - 8x^2 - 20.$$

Next, combine like terms:

$$3x^{10} - 3x^7 + 6x^3 - 4x^3 - 3x - 8x^2 + 21 - 20 = 3x^{10} - 3x^7 + 2x^3 - 3x - 8x^2 + 1.$$

Now, sum the coefficients:

$$3 - 3 + 2 - 3 - 8 + 1 = -8.$$

Therefore, the sum of the coefficients in the polynomial is $\boxed{-8}$.
