Problem:
Simplify the expression $$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac4{\sqrt{24}}+\dfrac{\sqrt{3456}}9+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt6}}.$$

Solution:
answer:  First, simplify the expression inside the square root:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac4{\sqrt{24}}+\dfrac{\sqrt{3456}}9+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}}$$

Simplify the fractions and square roots:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{4}{2\sqrt{6}}+\dfrac{58\sqrt{6}}{9}+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}}$$

Combine the terms in the numerator:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{2}{3}+\dfrac{58}{9}+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}}$$

Simplify the fractions:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{2}{3}+\dfrac{18}{3}+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}}$$

Combine the terms in the numerator:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{\dfrac{20}{3}+\sqrt{6}}{\sqrt{6}}}$$

Simplify the fraction:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{20}{3}+1}$$

Combine the terms:

$$\sqrt{\dfrac{23}{3}}$$

$$\boxed{\dfrac{23}{3}}$$
