Problem:
If $f(x)$ is a polynomial of degree 7, and $g(x)$ is a polynomial of degree 7, then what is the product of the minimum and the maximum possible degrees of $f(x) + g(x)$?

Solution:
answer:  The degree of the sum of two polynomials is the maximum of their degrees. Therefore, the maximum possible degree of $f(x) + g(x)$ is 7.

The minimum possible degree of $f(x) + g(x)$ occurs when $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are orthogonal polynomials. In this case, the degree of $f(x) + g(x)$ is 0.

Thus, the product of the minimum and the maximum possible degrees of $f(x) + g(x)$ is $0 \times 7 = \boxed{0}$.

