\[ 5 \text{ years} \times 2 \text{ periods per year} = 10 \text{ periods} \]

Next, we calculate the interest for each period. The interest rate is \(1\%\), so the interest for each period is:
\[ 24000 \times 0.01 = 240 \text{ dollars} \]

Since the interest is compounded bi-monthly, we need to add the interest for each period to the initial investment. After 10 periods, the total amount will be:
\[ 24000 \times (1.01)^{10} \]

