Problem:
Let \[f(x) =
\begin{cases}
|\lfloor{x}\rfloor| &\text{if }x\text{ is rational}, \\
\lceil{x}\rceil^2 &\text{if }x\text{ is irrational}.
\end{cases}
\] Find $f(\sqrt[3]{-8})+f(-\pi)+f(\sqrt{50})+f\left(\frac{9}{2}\right)$.

Solution:
answer:  We have that $f(\sqrt[3]{-8}) = \lceil{\sqrt[3]{-8}}\rceil^2 = \lceil{-2}\rceil^2 = 2^2 = 4$, $f(-\pi) = \lceil{\pi}\rceil^2 = \lceil{3}\rceil^2 = 3^2 = 9$, $f(\sqrt{50}) = \lceil{\sqrt{50}}\rceil^2 = \lceil{7}\rceil^2 = 7^2 = 49$, and $f\left(\frac{9}{2}\right) = \lfloor{\frac{9}{2}}\rfloor| = |\lfloor{4.5}\rfloor| = |4| = 4$. Therefore, the sum is $4 + 9 + 49 + 4 = \boxed{66}$.
