Problem:
Simplify $(2+3i)(1-2i)$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to simplify the expression:

{align*}
(2+3i)(1-2i) &= 2(1) + 2(-2i) + 3i(1) + 3i(-2i) \\
&= 2 - 4i + 3i - 6i^2 \\
&= 2 - 4i + 3i + 6 \\
&= 8 - 1i \\
&= \boxed{8 - i}.
\end{align*}
====================

