Problem:
For integers $n$, let \[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n^2 & \text{ if }n\text{ is odd}, \\
n^2 - 4n - 1 & \text{ if }n\text{ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f(f(f(f(f(4)))))$.

Solution:
answer:  First, we find $f(4)$:
\[f(4) = 4^2 - 4 \cdot 4 - 1 = 16 - 16 - 1 = -1.\]

Next, we find $f(f(4)) = f(-1)$:
\[f(-1) = (-1)^2 = 1.\]

Then, we find $f(f(f(4))) = f(1)$:
\[f(1) = 1^2 = 1.\]

Finally, we find $f(f(f(f(f(4)))) = f(1)$:
\[f(1) = 1^2 = 1.\]

Therefore, $f(f(f(f(f(4)))) = \boxed{1}$.
