Problem:
If \begin{align*}
4x-y+2z&=7,\\
6x+3y+3z&=5,
\end{align*} compute $y$.

Solution:
answer:  We can multiply the first equation by 3 to get $12x-3y+6z=21$. Subtracting this from the second equation, we get $6y=-16$, so $y=\boxed{-2}$.
