Problem:
If $x$, $y$, and $z$ are positive real numbers satisfying: \begin{align*}
\log x - \log y &= a, \\
\log y - \log z &= 15, \text{ and} \\
\log z - \log x &= -7, \\
\end{align*}where $a$ is a real number, what is $a$?

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the given equations as:
\begin{align*}
\log x - \log y &= a, \\
\log y - \log z &= 15, \\
\log z - \log x &= -7.
\end{align*}
Using the properties of logarithms, we can rewrite these equations as:
\begin{align*}
\log x - \log y &= a, \\
\log y - \log z &= 15, \\
\log z - \log x &= -7.
\end{align*}
Adding these three equations, we get:
\begin{align*}
\log x - \log y + \log y - \log z + \log z - \log x &= a + 15 + (-7) \\
0 &= a + 8 \\
\end{align*}
Solving for $a$, we get:
\begin{align*}
a &= -8.
\end{align*}
Therefore, $a = \boxed{-8}$.
