Problem:
A point with coordinates $(x,\ y)$ is randomly selected such that $0\leq x \leq10$ and $0\leq y \leq10$. What is the probability that the coordinates of the point will satisfy $2x+5y \geq 20$? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]

size(5cm,5cm);

draw((-2,0)--(12,0),Arrows);

draw((0,-2)--(0,12),Arrows);

pair a,b,x;

x=(0,0);

a=(10,0);

b=(0,10);

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.1,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.2,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.3,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.4,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.5,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.6,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.7,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.8,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,0.9,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--a,2,1,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.1,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.2,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.3,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.4,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.5,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.6,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.7,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.8,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,0.9,0,25));

add(pathticks(x--b,2,1,0,25));

[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the inequality $2x+5y \geq 20$ as $x+2.5y \geq 10$. This is the equation of a line with slope $-2.5$ and y-intercept $10$. The area above this line in the first quadrant is a triangle with vertices at $(0,0)$, $(10,0)$, and $(0,4)$. The area of this triangle is $\frac{1}{2} \cdot 10 \cdot 4 = 20$. The total area of the square is $10 \cdot 10 = 100$. Therefore, the probability is $\frac{20}{100} = \boxed{\frac{1}{5}}$.
