answer:  To determine the probability that Carson flips over the ace of spades before any face card, we need to consider the structure of the deck and the positions of the ace of spades and the face cards.

A standard 52-card deck has 12 face cards (jacks, queens, and kings) and the ace of spades. The ace of spades is the first card in the deck, and the first face card is the jack of spades, which is the 13th card in the deck.

