Problem:
A game of Plinko is played by dropping a ball at the top-middle of a set of pegs. Each time the ball hits a peg, it has a $\frac{1}{2}$ probability of deflecting either to the left or to the right. What is the probability that the ball lands in the middle slot as shown in the diagram (the red line)? [asy]
size(3inch, 2.25inch);
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i += 2) {

draw(circle((0, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((2, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((4, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((6, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((8, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((10, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((12, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((14, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((16, i + 1), 0.1));

draw(circle((1, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((3, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((5, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((7, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((9, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((11, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((13, i), 0.1));

draw(circle((15, i), 0.1));
}

pen target = red + linewidth(2);

draw((-0.8, -1)--(0.8, -1));
draw((1.2, -1)--(2.8, -1));
draw((3.2, -1)--(4.8, -1));
draw((5.2, -1)--(6.8, -1));
draw((7.2, -1)--(8.8, -1), target);
draw((9.2, -1)--(10.8, -1));
draw((11.2, -1)--(12.8, -1));
draw((13.2, -1)--(14.8, -1));
draw((15.2, -1)--(16.8, -1));

pen tube = black + linewidth(2);
draw((7.2, 9)--(7.2, 7.8)--(8.8, 7.8)--(8.8, 9), tube);

filldraw(Circle((8, 8.5), 0.6), blue);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  To determine the probability that the ball lands in the middle slot, we need to consider the probability of the ball hitting each peg and the subsequent deflection.

The ball starts at the top-middle of the set of pegs. Each time the ball hits a, it has a $\frac{1}{2}$ probability of deflecting either to the left or to the right.

The probability of the ball landing in the middle slot can be calculated by considering the sequence of hits and deflections. The ball must hit each peg in a specific order to land in the middle slot.

The probability of the ball hitting each peg in a specific order is the product of the probabilities of each individual hit and deflection. Since each hit and deflection is independent, the probability of each sequence is the product of the probabilities of each individual event.

The probability of the ball landing in the middle slot is the sum of the probabilities of all possible sequences of hits and deflections that lead to the middle slot.

Therefore, the probability that the ball lands in the middle slot is $\boxed{\frac{1}{16}}$.
