Solution:
answer:  First, we calculate the probability that Team A is selected on at least two of the next three days. We can do this by finding the probability that Team A is not selected on any of the next three days and subtracting it from 1.

The probability that Team A is not selected on any given day is $\frac{2}{3}$. Therefore, the probability that Team A is not selected on any of the next three days is $\left(\frac{2}{3}\right)^3 = \frac{8}{27}$.

