Problem:
$ABCDEFGH$ shown below is a right rectangular prism.  If the volume of pyramid $ABCH$ is 20, then what is the volume of $ABCDEFGH$?

[asy]

import three;

triple A,B,C,D,EE,F,G,H;

A = (0,0,0);

B = (5,0,0);

C = (5,6,0);

D= (0,6,0);

EE = (0,0,4);

F = B+EE;

G = C + EE;

H = D + EE;

draw(B--C--D);

draw(B--A--D,dashed);

draw(EE--F--G--H--EE);

draw(A--EE,dashed);

draw(B--F);

draw(C--G);

draw(D--H);

label("$A$",A,S);

label("$B$",B,W);

label("$C$",C,S);

label("$D$",D,E);

label("$E$",EE,N);

label("$F$",F,W);

label("$G$",G,SW);

label("$H$",H,E);

[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  The volume of a pyramid is given by the formula $\frac{1}{3} \times \text{Base Area} \times \text{Height}$. In this case, the base of the pyramid is triangle $ABC$ and the height is the distance from $C$ to the plane containing $ABC$. Since the volume of the pyramid is 20, we have:

$$\frac{1}{3} \times \text{Base Area} \times \text{Height} = 20.$$

The volume of the right rectangular prism $ABCDEFGH$ is given by the formula $\text{Base Area} \times \text{Height}$. In this case, the base of the prism is triangle $ABC$ and the height is the distance from $C$ to the plane containing $ABC$. Since the volume of the prism is equal to the volume of the pyramid, we have:

$$\text{Base Area} \times \text{Height} = 60.$$

Therefore, the volume of the right rectangular prism $ABCDEFGH$ is $\boxed{60}$.
