Problem:
In the diagram, what is the area of $\triangle ABC$? [asy]
size(5cm);
real xmax = 15; real ymax = 13; real xmin = -3; real ymin = -3;
pair a = (4, 9); pair b = (0, 0); pair c = (12, 0); draw(b--a--c);
draw((xmin, 0)--(xmax, 0), Arrow); label("$x$", (xmax, 0), E);
draw((0, ymin)--(0, ymax), Arrow); label("$y$", (0, ymax), N);
label("$B(0, 0)$", b, SW);
label("$C(12, 0)$", c, S);
label("$A(4, 9)$", a, N);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  The area of $\triangle ABC$ can be found using the formula for the area of a triangle given its vertices:

$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|$$

Substituting the coordinates of the vertices, we have:

$$\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 4(0 - 0) + 0(0 - 9) + 12(9 - 0) \right| = \frac{1}{2} \left| 0 + 0 + 108 \right| = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 108 = \boxed{54}$$

Final Answer: The final answer is $54$. I hope it is correct.
