Problem:
If the point $(3,4)$ is reflected in the $x$-axis, what are the coordinates of its image?

[asy]
draw((-5.5,0)--(5.5,0),linewidth(1));
draw((-5.5,0)--(5.5,0),EndArrow);
draw((0,-5.5)--(0,5.5),EndArrow);
draw((0,-5.5)--(0,5.5),linewidth(1));
draw((-5,-5)--(-5,5)--(5,5)--(5,-5)--cycle);
draw((-4,-5)--(-4,5));
draw((-3,-5)--(-3,5));
draw((-2,-5)--(-2,5));
draw((-1,-5)--(-1,5));
draw((1,-5)--(1,5));
draw((2,-5)--(2,5));
draw((3,-5)--(3,5));
draw((4,-5)--(4,5));
draw((-5,-4)--(5,-4));
draw((-5,-3)--(5,-3));
draw((-5,-2)--(5,-2));
draw((-5,-1)--(5,-1));
draw((-5,1)--(5,1));
draw((-5,2)--(5,2));
draw((-5,3)--(5,3));
draw((-5,4)--(5,4));
dot((3,4));
label("$x$",(5.5,0),E);
label("$y$",(0,5.5),N);
label("$(3,4)$",(3,4),NE);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  To reflect a point in the \(x\)-axis, we change the sign of the \(y\)-coordinate while keeping the \(x\)-coordinate the same. Therefore, the coordinates of the image of \((3,4)\) in the \(x\)-axis are \((3,-4)\).

\(\boxed{(3,-4)}\)
