Problem:
Quadrilateral MNPQ has vertices with coordinates $M(2,5)$, $N(6, 5)$, $P(6, 7)$ and $Q(2, 7)$. When the figure is rotated clockwise $270^\circ$ around point $M$ and then reflected across the line $x = 1$, what are the coordinates of the final image of point $Q$? Express your answer as an ordered pair.

Solution:
answer:  First, we rotate point $Q(2, 7)$ clockwise $270^\circ$ around point $M(2, 5)$. The coordinates of $Q$ after this rotation are $(-7, -2)$.

Next, we reflect point $Q$ across the line $x = 1$. The coordinates of $Q$ after this reflection are $(-7, -2)$.

Therefore, the coordinates of the final image of point $Q$ are $\boxed{(-7, -2)}$.
