Problem:
A sequence of numbers $a_1,$ $a_2,$ $a_3,$ $a_4,$ $\dots,$ has the property that each term after the first is one less than the product of its two neighbors.  If $a_1 = 1492$ and $a_2 = 1776,$ then determine $a_{2003}.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that $a_3 = a_1a_2 - 1 = 1492 \cdot 1776 - 1 = 265,471$. Then, $a_4 = a_2a_3 - 1 = 1776 \cdot 265,471 - 1 = 470,099,395$. Finally, $a_5 = a_3a_4 - 1 = 265,471 \cdot 470,099,395 - 1 = 125,471,470,099,144$. Therefore, $a_{2003} = a_3 = \boxed{265,471}$.
====================

