Problem:
Simplify
\[\left( \frac{3 + i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8 + \left( \frac{3 - i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can use the fact that $\left( \frac{3 + i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right) + \left( \frac{3 - i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right) = 3$ and $\left( \frac{3 + i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right) \left( \frac{3 - i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right) = 3.$ Therefore, we have

\[\left( \frac{3 + i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8 + \left( \frac{3 - i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8 = \left( \frac{3 + i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8 + \left( \frac{3 - i \sqrt{3}}{2} \right)^8 = \boxed{6}.\]
