Problem:
Let $F(z)=\frac{z+i}{z-i}$ for all complex numbers $z\not= i,$ and let $z_n=F(z_{n-1})$ for all positive integers $n.$ Given that $z_0=\frac 1{137}+i,$ find $z_{2002}.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that $F(z)=\frac{z+i}{z-i}=\frac{z+i}{z+i}=1$ for all $z\not= i$. Therefore, $z_n=F(z_{n-1})=1$ for all positive integers $n$. Hence, $z_{2002}=1$.
\boxed{1}
