Problem:
Find the remainder when $3y^4-4y^3+5y^2-13y+4$ is divided by $3y - 2.$

Solution:
answer:  We can use polynomial long division to find the remainder.

\begin{align*}
3y^4 - 4y^3 + 5y^2 - 13y + 4 \div (3y - 2) &= y^3 - 2y^2 + 3y - 1 + \frac{2y^3 - 4y^2 - 7y + 4}{3y - 2} \\
&= y^3 - 2y^2 + 3y - 1 + \frac{2y^3 - 4y^2 - 7y + 4}{3y - 2} \\
&= y^3 - 2y^2 + 3y - 1 + \frac{2y^3 - 4y^2 - 7y + 4}{3y - 2} \\
&= y^3 - 2y^2 + 3y - 1 + \frac{2y^3 - 4y^2 - 7y + 4}{3y - 2} \\
&= \boxed{2y^2 - 3y}.
\end{align*}
