Solution:
answer:  We can use the Remainder Theorem to find the remainder when $f(x)$ is divided by $x^2-1$. The Remainder Theorem states that the remainder of the division of $f(x)$ by $x-a$ is $f(a)$.

In this case, we want to find the remainder when $f(x)$ is divided by $x^2-1$, which is equivalent to finding the remainder when $f(x)$ is divided by $(x-1)(x+1)$.

