answer:  We can rewrite the equation as
\[(12x - 1)(6x - 1)(4x - 1)(3x - 1) - 5 = 0.\]This equation has four factors, so it has at most four real roots. We can use the Rational Root Theorem to find possible rational roots, but in this case, we can use numerical methods to find the roots.

