Problem:
If $z^2 + z + 1 = 0,$ find
\[z^{49} + z^{50} + z^{51} + z^{52} + z^{53}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We know that $z^2 + z + 1 = 0,$ so $z^3 = -z - 1.$ Therefore, $z^4 = z^3 \cdot z = (-z - 1) \cdot z = -z^2 - z.$ Similarly, $z^5 = z^4 \cdot z = (-z^2 - z) \cdot z = -z^3 - z^2 = -z - 1.$ Also, $z^6 = z^5 \cdot z = (-z - 1) \cdot z = -z^2 - z.$ Finally, $z^7 = z^6 \cdot z = (-z^2 - z) \cdot z = -z^3 - z^2 = -z - 1.$ Therefore, $z^{49} + z^{50} + z^{51} + z^{52} + z^{53} = z^3 + z^4 + z^5 + z^6 + z^7 = -z - 1 + (-z^2 - z) + (-z - 1) - z - 1 = \boxed{-5}.$
====================

