Problem:
Let $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ be nonnegative real numbers such that $x + y + z = 3.$  Find the maximum value of
\[(xy + z)(xz + y).\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that $(xy + z)(xz + y) = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy(x + y + z) + zx(x + y + z) + yz + zx = xy
