Problem:
Compute
\[\sum_{k = 1}^\infty \frac{k + 2}{k! + (k + 1)! + (k + 2)!}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression inside the sum as

$$\frac{k + 2}{k! + (k + 1)! + (k + 2)!} = \frac{k + 2}{(k + 1)(k + 2)} = \frac{1}{k + 1} - \frac{1}{k + 2}.$$

Thus, the sum becomes

$$\sum_{k = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{k + 1} - \frac{1}{k + 2} \right) = \left( \frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{3} \right) + \left( \frac{1}{3} - \frac{1}{4} \right) + \left( \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{5} \right) + \cdots.$$

This is a telescoping series, so the sum simplifies to

$$1 - \frac{1}{2} = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}.$$
====================

