Problem:
The sequence $(a_n)$ is defined by $a_0 = 2,$ $a_1 = 1,$ and
\[a_n = a_{n - 1} \sqrt{3} - a_{n - 2}\]for all $n \ge 2.$  Find $a_{100}.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that $a_2 = a_1 \sqrt{3} - a_0 = 1 \sqrt{3} - 2 = \sqrt{3} - 2,$ and $a_3 = a_2 \sqrt{3} - a_1 = (\sqrt{3} - 2) \sqrt{3} - 1 = 3 - 2 - 1 = 0.$ Similarly, $a_4 = a_3 \sqrt{3} - a_2 = 0 \sqrt{3} - (\sqrt{3} - 2) = -\sqrt{3} + 2,$ and $a_5 = a_4 \sqrt{3} - a_3 = (-\sqrt{3} + 2) \sqrt{3} - 0 = 3 - 2 = 1.$ We see that the sequence is periodic with period 3. Therefore, $a_{100} = a_1 = \boxed{1}.$
