Problem:
The positive integers up to 2007 are alternately subtracted and added:
\[1 - 2 + 3 - 4 + \cdots + 2001 - 2002 + 2003 - 2004 + 2005 - 2006 + 2007.\]What is the value of the expression?

Solution:
answer:  We can group the terms in pairs:
\[(1 - 2) + (3 - 4) + (5 - 6) + \cdots + (2001 - 2002) + (2003 - 2004) + (2005 - 2006) + 2007.\]
Each pair sums to $-1$, and there are $1003$ pairs plus the last term $2007$. Therefore, the sum of the expression is:
\[1003 \cdot (-1) + 2007 = -1003 + 2007 = \boxed{1004}.\]
