Problem:
For positive real numbers $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d,$ find the minimum value of
\[\left\lfloor \frac{b + c + d}{a} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + c + d}{b} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + d}{c} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + c}{d} \right\rfloor.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[\left\lfloor \frac{b + c + d}{a} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + c + d}{b} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + d}{c} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + c}{d} \right\rfloor \ge 3 \left\lfloor \frac{b + c + d}{a} \right\rfloor + 3 \left\lfloor \frac{a + c + d}{b} \right\rfloor + 3 \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + d}{c} \right\rfloor + 3 \left\lfloor \frac{a + b + c}{d} \right\rfloor = 12.\]
Equality occurs when $a = b = c = d,$ so the minimum value is $\boxed{12}.$
