Problem:
For real numbers $x$ and $y,$ find all possible values of
\[\lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor.\]Enter all possible values, separated by commas.

Solution:
answer:  We know that $\lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor$ can be expressed as $\lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \lfloor x + y \rfloor - \lfloor x \rfloor - \lfloor y \rfloor = \boxed{0}$.
