Problem:
Compute the product
\[\frac{(1998^2 - 1996^2)(1998^2 - 1995^2) \dotsm (1998^2 - 0^2)}{(1997^2 - 1996^2)(1997^2 - 1995^2) \dotsm (1997^2 - 0^2)}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression as

\[\frac{(1998-1996)(1998-1995) \dotsm (1998-0)}{1997\cdot (1997-1996)(1997-1995) \dotsm (1997-0)} = \frac{1998\cdot 1997\cdot 1996\cdot \dotsm 1}{1997\cdot 1996\cdot 1995\cdot \dotsm 1} = \frac{1998}{1997} = \boxed{1}.\]
