answer:  The given polynomial is a polynomial of degree 2001. To determine the number of real roots, we can use the fact that a polynomial of degree \( n \) can have at most \( n \) real roots, counting multiplicities. Here, the degree of the polynomial is 2001, so it can have at most 2001 real roots.

Therefore, the number of real roots of the polynomial is \(\boxed{2001}\).
