This implies that

\[\frac{x + 1}{x + 2} + \frac{x + 8}{x + 9} = \frac{x + 2}{x + 3} + \frac{x + 7}{x + 8}.\]

Since the left-hand side and the right-hand side are equal, the equation is true for all values of $x$. Therefore, the solution is

\[\boxed{\text{all real numbers}}.\]
