Problem:
Compute the smallest positive integer $x$ greater than 9 such that
\[\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = 9 = \lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that $\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = 9$ and $\lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor = 9$. This means that $\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = \lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor = 9$. Therefore, $\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = 9$ and $\lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor = 9$. This implies that $\lfloor x \rfloor - 19 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{19} \right\rfloor = \lfloor x \rfloor - 89 \left\lfloor \frac{x}{89} \right\rfloor = 9$. Therefore, the smallest positive integer $x$ greater than 9 that satisfies the equation is $\boxed{9}$.
