Problem:
Which of the following polynomials has the greatest real root?

(A) $x^{19}+2018x^{11}+1$
(B) $x^{17}+2018x^{11}+1$
(C) $x^{19}+2018x^{13}+1$
(D) $x^{17}+2018x^{13}+1$
(E) $2019x+2018$

Enter the letter of the polynomial with the greatest real root.

Solution:
answer:  To determine which polynomial has the greatest real root, we need to analyze the degrees of the polynomials. The degree of a polynomial is the highest power of \( x \) with a non-zero coefficient.

(A) \( x^{19} + 2018x^{11} + 1 \)
(B) \( x^{17} + 2018x^{11} + 1 \)
(C) \( x^{19} + 2018x^{13} + 1 \)
(D) \( x^{17} + 2018x^{13} + 1 \)
(E) \( 2019x + 2018 \)

The degree of polynomial (A) is 19.
The degree of polynomial (B) is 17.
The degree of polynomial (C) is 19.
The degree of polynomial (D) is 17.
The degree of polynomial (E) is 1.

The polynomial with the greatest degree is (C).

Therefore, the final answer is \(\boxed{C}\).
