Problem:
There exist constants $r,$ $s,$ and $t$ so that
\[p(n) = rp(n - 1) + sp(n - 2) + tp(n - 3)\]for any quadratic polynomial $p(x),$ and any integer $n.$  Enter the ordered triple $(r,s,t).$

Solution:
answer:  Let $p(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.$  Then
\begin{align*}
p(n) &= an^2 + bn + c, \\
p(n - 1) &= a(n - 1)^2 + b(n - 1) + c, \\
p(n - 2) &= a(n - 2)^2 + b(n - 2) + c, \\
p(n - 3) &= a(n - 3)^2 + b(n - 3) + c.
\end{align*}
Expanding, we get
\[an^2 + bn + c = r(an^2 - 2an + 1) + s(an^2 - 4an + 4) + t(an^2 - 6an + 9).\]
Comparing coefficients, we find that $r = 1,$ $s = 2,$ and $t = 3.$
Thus, the ordered triple $(r,s,t)$ is $\boxed{(1,2,3)}.$
