Problem:
For a complex number $z,$ find the minimum value of
\[|z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 + 2i|^2 + |z - 1 + i|^2.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the given expression as
\[|z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 + 2i|^2 + |z - 1 + i|^2 = |z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 - 2i|^2 + |z - 1 - i|^2.\]
By the triangle inequality, we have
\[|z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 - 2i|^2 + |z - 1 - i|^2 \ge |z - 3|^2 + |z - 5 - 2i|^2 + |z - 1 - i|^2 = 3z^2 - 18z + 29.\]
Therefore, the minimum value of the expression is $\boxed{29}$.
