Problem:
Multiply $(x^6 -19x^3 + 361) (x^3+19)$.

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to multiply the two polynomials:

\begin{align*}
(x^6 - 19x^3 + 361)(x^3 + 19) &= x^6(x^3 + 19) - 19x^3(x^3 + 19) + 361(x^3 + 19) \\
&= x^9 + 19x^6 - 19x^6 - 38x x^3 + 19x^3 + 6859 \\
&= x^9 + 0x^6 - 38x x^3 + 6859 \\
&= x^9 - 38x x^3 + 6859.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the answer is $\boxed{x^9 - 38x^3 + 6859}$.
