Problem:
Compute
\[\sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{(\sqrt{n} + \sqrt{n + 1})(\sqrt[4]{n} + \sqrt[4]{n + 1})}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the sum as

\[\sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{(\sqrt{n} + \sqrt{n + 1})(\sqrt[4]{n} + \sqrt[4]{n + 1})} = \sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n} + \sqrt{n + 1}} - \sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{\sqrt[4]{n} + \sqrt[4]{n + 1}}.\]

We can simplify the first term as

\[\sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n} + \sqrt{n + 1}} = \sum_{n = 1}^{9999} \frac{1}{\sqrt{n} + \sqrt{n + 1}} = \boxed{0}.\]
