Problem:
Find the real roots of
\[\frac{( x+ 1)(x - 3)}{5(x + 2)(x - 4)} + \frac{(x + 3)(x - 5)}{9(x + 4)(x - 6)} - \frac{2(x + 5)(x - 7)}{13(x + 6)(x - 8)} = \frac{92}{585}.\]Enter the real roots, separated by commas.

Solution:
answer:  First, we combine the fractions on the left side of the equation by finding a common denominator. The common denominator is $5(x + 2)(x - 4)9(x + 4)(x - 6)13(x + 6)(x - 8)$. We then multiply both sides by this common denominator to clear the fractions. This gives us

\[5(x + 2)(x - 4)9(x + 4)(x - 6)13(x + 6)(x - 8) = 92(x + 2)(x - 4)9(x + 4)(x - 6)13(x + 6)(x - 8).\]

Simplifying, we get

\[0 = 87(x + 2)(x - 4)9(x + 4)(x - 6)13(x + 6)(x - 8).\]

This equation is never true for any value of $x$. Therefore, there are no real roots to the equation.

\boxed{\text{No solution}}
