Problem:
Evaluate the expression \[(751 - 745) + (748 - 742) + (745 - 739) + (742 - 736) + \cdots + (499 - 493) + (496 - 490).\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression as follows:

\[(751 - 745) + (748 - 742) + (745 - 739) + (742 - 736) + \cdots + (499 - 493) + (496 - 490) = 6 + 6 + 6 + 6 + \cdots + 6 + 6.\]

There are 11 terms in this sum, each equal to 6. Therefore, the sum is:

\[11 \times 6 = \boxed{66}.\]
