Problem:
What is the value of the following expression: $100 - 99 +98 - 97 + 96 - 95 + \cdots + 4 - 3 +2 - 1$?

Solution:
answer:  We can pair the terms in the expression as follows:

$$(100 - 99) + (98 - 97) + (96 - 95) + \cdots + (4 - 3) + (2 - 1)$$

Each pair of terms sums to $-1$. Therefore, the value of the expression is:

$$-1 + -1 + -1 + \cdots + -1 = \boxed{-50}$$
