Problem:
Given that \begin{align*}x_{1}&=211,\\ x_{2}&=375,\\ x_{3}&=420,\\ x_{4}&=523,\ \text{and}\\ x_{n}&=x_{n-1}-x_{n-2}+x_{n-3}-x_{n-4}\ \text{when}\ n\geq5, \end{align*}find the value of $x_{531}+x_{753}+x_{975}$.

Solution:
answer:  We can see that the sequence $x_n$ is periodic with period 4. Therefore, $x_{531}=x_3$, $x_{753}=x_1$, and $x_{975}=x_2$. Thus, we have

$$x_{531}+x_{753}+x_{975}=x_3+x_1+x_2=420+211+375=\boxed{1006}.$$
