Problem:
Find all real numbers $x$ such that \[\left(\frac{x}{2x-1}\right)^2 \le 9.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that

$$\left(\frac{x}{2x-1}\right)^2 \le 9 \Rightarrow \frac{x}{2x-1} \le 3.$$

This inequality is satisfied when $x \in \boxed{(-\infty, \frac{1}{2}] \cup [\frac{3}{2}, \infty)}.$
