Problem:
What is the product (in base 10) of the first and last digits of the base-6 representation of $682_{10}$?

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to convert $682_{10}$ to base-6. We do this by repeatedly dividing the number by 6 and recording the remainders.

\begin{align*}
682 \div 6 &= 113 \text{ remainder } 4 \\
113 \div 6 &= 19 \text{ remainder } 1 \\
19 \div 6 &= 3 \text{ remainder } 1 \\
3 \div 6 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 3 \\
\end{align*}

Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base-6 representation of $682_{10}$ as $3114_6$.

The first digit of $3114_6$ is $3$ and the last digit is $4$. The product of these two digits is:

\[3 \times 4 = 12\]

Therefore, the product of the first and last digits of the base-6 representation of $682_{10}$ is $\boxed{12}$.
