Problem:
Find the remainder when $24^{50} - 15^{50}$ is divided by 13.

Solution:
answer:  We can use modular arithmetic to simplify the problem. First, we find the remainder when $24^{50}$ is divided by 13. Since $24 \equiv 1 \pmod{13}$, we have $24^{50} \equiv 1^{50} \equiv 1 \pmod{13}$. Next, we find the remainder when $15^{50}$ is divided by 13. Since $15 \equiv 2 \pmod{13}$, we have $15^{50} \equiv 2^{50} \equiv 4 \pmod{13}$. Therefore, we have $24^{50} - 15^{50} \equiv 1 - 4 \equiv -3 \pmod{13}$. Since we want a positive remainder, we add 13 to $-3$ to get $10$. Therefore, the remainder is $\boxed{10}$.
