Problem:
What is the greatest common divisor of all of the members of the set containing all numbers that are the product of four consecutive positive integers?

Solution:
answer:  Let the four consecutive positive integers be $n$, $n+1$, $n+2$, and $n+3$. The product is $n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)$. We can rewrite this as $n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = \boxed{6}$.

Final Answer: The final answer is $6$. I hope it is correct.
