Problem:
How many digits are in the whole-number representation of $10^{100}-9^{100}$?

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite $10^{100}-9^{100}$ as $10^{100}(10-9) = 10^{100} \cdot 1 = 10^{100}$. The number $10^{100}$ has 101 digits. Therefore, the number of digits in the whole-number representation of $10^{100}-9^{100}$ is $\boxed{101}$.
