Problem:
If the pattern shown continues, what is the letter in the $2010$th position? MATHLETEMATHLETEMATHLETE...

Solution:
answer:  To determine the letter in the 2010th position of the sequence "MATHLETEMATHLETEMATHLETE...", we need to identify the pattern in the sequence.

The sequence is "MATHLETE MATHLETE MATHLETE MATHLETE ...". We can see that the word "MATHLETE" is repeated indefinitely.

The length of the word "MATHLETE" is 8 characters.

To find the position of the 2010th character within one cycle of "MATHLETE", we calculate the remainder when 2010 is divided by 8:

\[ 2010 \div 8 = 252 \text{ remainder } 2 \]

The remainder is 2, which means the 2010th character corresponds to the 2nd character in the word "MATHLETE".

The 2nd character in "MATHLETE" is 'T'.

Therefore, the letter in the 2010th position is \(\boxed{T}\).
