Problem:
If $$\begin{array}{@{}l@{\;}l@{}l@{}l} && & P_b \\ & \times & & P_b \\ \cline{2-4} & & 3 & 1_b, \\ \end{array} $$where $P$ and $b$ represent two distinct digits 0-9 and $P$ is one less than $b$, what is the value of the base $b$?

Solution:
answer:  Let $P = b - 1$. Then we have

$$(b-1)(b-1) = 31_b.$$

Converting $31_b$ to base 10, we get

$$31_b = 3b + 1 = 4.$$

So, we have

$$(b-1)(b-1) = 4.$$

Expanding and simplifying, we get

$$b^2 - 2b + 1 = 4.$$

Rearranging, we get

$$b^2 - 2b - 3 = 0.$$

Factoring, we get

$$(b-3)(b+1) = 0.$$

So, $b = 3$ or $b = -1$. Since $b$ must be a positive integer, we have $b = 3$.

\boxed{3}
