Problem:
Arnold must water his cactus plants every 9 days and he must feed them every 60 days. He watered and fed them last Tuesday. What day of the week will it be the next time he waters and feeds them on the same day?

Solution:
answer:  To determine the next day of the week when Arnold will water and feed his cactus plants on the same day, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of the watering and feeding intervals.

The watering interval is 9 days, and the feeding interval is 60 days.

First, we find the LCM of 9 and 60:

The LCM of 9 and 60 is 180.

Next, we need to determine the day of the week it will be 180 days after Tuesday.

We do this by finding the remainder when 180 is divided by 7:

\[180 \div 7 = 26 \text{ remainder } 2\]

This means that 180 days is equivalent to 26 weeks and 2 days.

Since 26 weeks is exactly another Tuesday, adding 2 days to Tuesday gives us Thursday.

Therefore, the next time Arnold will water and feed his cactus plants on the same day will be on \(\boxed{\text{Thursday}}\).
