Problem:
The Fibonacci sequence is the sequence 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, $\ldots$ where each term is the sum of the previous two terms. What is the remainder when the $100^{\mathrm{th}}$ term of the sequence is divided by 4?

Solution:
answer:  The Fibonacci sequence repeats every 12 terms, so we can find the remainder of the $100^{\mathrm{th}}$ term when dividing by 4 by finding the remainder of the $10^{\mathrm{th}}$ term when dividing by 4.

The $10^{\mathrm{th}}$ term of the Fibonacci sequence is $55$. To find the remainder when $55$ is divided by $4$, we perform the division:

$$55 \div 4 = 13 \text{ remainder } 3$$

Therefore, the remainder when the $100^{\mathrm{th}}$ term of the sequence is divided by 4 is $\boxed{3}$.
====================

