Problem:
What is the remainder when $225^{66}-327^{66}$ is divided by $17$?

Solution:
answer:  We can use modular arithmetic to simplify the problem. First, we find the remainder of $225$ and $327$ when divided by $17$:

$$225 \equiv 8 \pmod{17}$$
$$327 \equiv 15 \pmod{17}$$

Now, we substitute these remainders into the expression:

$$225^{66} - 327^{66} \equiv 8^{66} - 15^{66} \pmod{17}$$

Next, we simplify the expression using properties of modular arithmetic:

$$8^{66} \equiv 1 \pmod{17}$$
$$15^{66} \equiv 1 \pmod{17}$$

Therefore, the expression becomes:

$$1 - (-1) \equiv 0 \pmod{17}$$

So, the remainder when $225^{66} - 327^{66}$ is divided by $17$ is $\boxed{0}$.
