Problem:
For a world record, George Adrian picked 15,832 pounds of apples in 8 hours. Assuming he maintained a constant rate of picking, how many pounds of apples did he pick in 3 hours?

Solution:
answer:  To determine how many pounds of apples George Adrian picked in 3 hours, we first need to find his rate of picking apples per hour. He picked 15,832 pounds in 8 hours, so his rate is:

\[
\text{Rate} = \frac{15832 \text{ pounds}}{8 \text{ hours}} = 1979 \text{ pounds per hour}
\]

Next, we use this rate to find out how many pounds he picked in 3 hours:

\[
\text{Pounds picked in 3 hours} = 1979 \text{ pounds per hour} \times 3 \text{ hours} = 5937 \text{ pounds}
\]

Therefore, George Adrian picked \boxed{5937} pounds of apples in 3 hours.
