Problem:
Evaluate $\sqrt{5\cdot10\cdot14\cdot21\cdot15\cdot20}$.

Solution:
answer:  We can simplify the expression inside the square root by factoring out the common factors:

$$5\cdot10\cdot14\cdot21\cdot15\cdot20 = (5\cdot2)\cdot(5\cdot2)\cdot(2\cdot7)\cdot(3\cdot7)\cdot(5\cdot3)\cdot(2\cdot2\cdot5)$$

$$= 5^2\cdot2^2\cdot3^2\cdot7^2$$

$$= 25\cdot4\cdot9\cdot49$$

$$= 25\cdot36\cdot49$$

$$= 900\cdot49$$

$$= 44100$$

Therefore, the expression simplifies to:

$$\sqrt{44100} = \boxed{210}$$
