Problem:
A stock loses $10\%$ of its value on Monday.  On Tuesday it loses  $20\%$ of the value it had at the end of the day on Monday.  What is  the overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to  the end of Tuesday?  Enter the answer as a percent.

Solution:
answer:  Let the initial value of the stock be \( V \).

On Monday, the stock loses 10% of its value, so the value at the end of Monday is:
\[ V - 0.1V = 0.9V. \]

On Tuesday, the stock loses 20% of the value it had at the end of Monday, so the value at the end of Tuesday is:
\[ 0.9V - 0.2 \times 0.9V = 0.9V - 0.18V = 0.72V. \]

The overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to the end of Tuesday is:
\[ V - 0.72V = 0.28V. \]

The overall percent loss is:
\[ \left( \frac{0.28V}{V} \right) \times 100\% = 28\% \]

Therefore, the overall percent loss in value from the beginning of Monday to the end of Tuesday is \(\boxed{28\%}\).
====================

