The arithmetic mean of eight positive integers is 7. If one of the eight integers is removed, the mean becomes 6. What is the value of the integer that is removed?

Solution:
answer:  The arithmetic mean of the eight integers is 7, so the sum of the eight integers is $7 \times 8 = 56$.

When one integer is removed, the mean becomes 6, so the sum of the remaining seven integers is $6 \times 7 = 42$.

Therefore, the value of the removed that integer is $56 - 42 = \boxed{14}$.

