Problem:
The measure of an interior angle of a regular decagon is how many degrees greater than the measure of an interior angle of a regular pentagon?

Solution:
answer:  The measure of an interior angle of a regular decagon is $180(10-2)/10=180(8)/10=144$ degrees. The measure of an interior angle of a regular pentagon is $180(5-2)/5=180(3)/5=108$ degrees. Therefore, the measure of an interior angle of a regular decagon is $144-108=\boxed{36}$ degrees greater than the measure of an interior angle of a regular pentagon.
