Problem:
Three identical squares are placed side by side to form a rectangle with a perimeter of 104 inches. What is the area, in square inches, of each square?

[asy]
size(150);
pair x = (2,0);
draw((-1,-1)-- (1,-1)--(1,1)--(-1,1)--cycle);
draw((-1,-1)+x-- (1,-1)+x--(1,1)+x--(-1,1)+x--cycle);
draw((-1,-1)-x-- (1,-1)-x--(1,1)-x--(-1,1)-x--cycle);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  Let the side length of each square be \( s \). Since three squares are placed side by side, the length of the rectangle is \( 3s \) and the width is \( s \).

The perimeter of the rectangle is given by the formula:
\[
\text{Perimeter} = 2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width})
\]
Substituting the given dimensions:
\[
104 = 2 \times (3s + s)
\]
\[
104 = 2 \times 4s
\]
\[
104 = 8s
\]
\[
s = \frac{104}{8}
\]
\[
s = 13
\]

The area of each square is:
\[
\text{Area} = s^2 = 13^2 = 169
\]

Therefore, the area of each square is \(\boxed{169}\) square inches.
====================

====================
