Problem:
How many six-inch by six-inch square tiles are needed to cover a three-foot by two-foot rectangular section of floor?

Solution:
answer:  First, convert the dimensions of the rectangular section from feet to inches:
- 3 feet = \(3 \times 12 = 36\) inches
- 2 feet = \(2 \times 12 = 24\) inches

Next, calculate the area of the rectangular section in square inches:
- Area of the rectangular section = \(36 \times 24 = 864\) square inches

Now, calculate the area of one six-inch by six-inch square tile:
- Area of one tile = \(6 \times 6 = 36\) square inches

Finally, determine the number of tiles needed by dividing the area of the rectangular section by the area of one tile:
- Number of tiles = \(\frac{864}{36} = 24\)

Therefore, the number of six-inch by six-inch square tiles needed to cover the three-foot by two-foot rectangular section of floor is \(\boxed{24}\).
====================

