Problem:
A 10-by-12-inch page has margins of 1.5 inches on all sides. What fraction of the area of the page is taken up by the margins? Express your answer as a common fraction.

Solution:
answer:  The area of the entire page is $10 \times 12 = 120$ square inches. The area of the page without the margins is $7.5 \times 9.5 = 71.25$ square inches. Therefore, the area taken up by the margins is $120 - 71.25 = 48.75$ square inches. The fraction of the area taken up by the margins is $\frac{48.75}{120} = \boxed{\frac{3}{8}}$.
