Problem:
A stairway with three steps has three risers that are each 8 inches high and three treads that are each 10 inches deep. What is the area, in square inches, of this figure that is the side panel of the stairway?

[asy]size(101);
real textsize = 10pt;
draw((0,0)--(30,0)--(30,8)--(20,8)--(20,16)--(10,16)--(10,24)--(0,24)--cycle);
draw((31,0)--(33,0)^^(32,0)--(32,8)^^(31,8)--(33,8));
label("$8''$ riser",(33,4),E,fontsize(textsize));
draw((10,25)--(10,27)^^(10,26)--(20,26)^^(20,25)--(20,27));
label("$10''$",(15,27),N,fontsize(textsize));
label("tread",(15,32),N,fontsize(textsize));[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  To find the area of the side panel of the stairway, we need to calculate the area of the rectangle formed by the risers and treads.

The height of the rectangle is the sum of the heights of the three risers:
\[ 3 \times 8 = 24 \text{ inches} \]

The width of the rectangle is the sum of the depths of the three treads:
\[ 3 \times 10 = 30 \text{ inches} \]

The area of the rectangle is given by the product of its height and width:
\[ 24 \times 30 = 720 \text{ square inches} \]

Therefore, the area of the side panel of the stairway is:
\[ \boxed{720} \]
