Problem:
Eleven rectangular 9-inch by 12-inch pictures hang on a wall. How many square inches of the wall's surface area are covered by the pictures?

Solution:
answer:  To determine the total area of the wall's surface area covered by the pictures, we first need to calculate the area of one picture and then multiply it by the number of pictures.

The area of one picture is given by the product of its length and width:
\[
\text{Area of one picture} = 9 \, \text{inches} \times 12 \, \text{inches} = 108 \, \text{square inches}
\]

Since there are eleven pictures, the total area covered by the pictures is:
\[
\text{Total area} = 11 \times 108 \, \text{square inches} = 1188 \, \text{square inches}
\]

Therefore, the total area of the wall's surface area covered by the pictures is \boxed{1188} square inches.
====================

