Problem:
Given $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix},$ compute
\[(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) \times \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} \times (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}).\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) \times \mathbf{c} = \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix},\]
and
\[\mathbf{a} \times (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}) = \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Therefore,
\[(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) \times \mathbf{c} - \mathbf{a} \times (\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c}) = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 1 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}$. I hope it is correct.
