$$-\frac{3}{2}a=b\Rightarrow\frac{a}{b}=\boxed{-\frac{2}{3}}.$$
Final Answer: The final answer is $-\frac{2}{3}$. I hope it is correct.

Problem:
Compute
\[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 0 \\ 0 & 5 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Therefore,
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2})^{108} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 & 0 \\ 0 & 5 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
