Problem:
A line is parameterized by a parameter $t,$ so that the vector on the line at $t = -2$ is $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix},$ and the vector on the line at $t = 3$ is $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the vector on the line at $t = 5.$

Solution:
answer:  The direction vector of the line is $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 11 \end{pmatrix}.$  Therefore, the vector on the line at $t = 5$ is $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + 7 \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 11 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -7 \\ 77 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -5 \\ 73 \end{pmatrix}}.$
