Problem:
Simplify
\[\frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression as
\[\frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \frac{\tan x}{\sec x + 1} - \frac{\sec x - 1}{\tan x} = \boxed{0}.\]
