Problem:
Find the matrix $\mathbf{L} = \begin{pmatrix} a & 0 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}$ such that $a > 0,$ $d > 0,$ and
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & 0 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & c \\ 0 & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & -6 \\ -6 & 34 \end{pmatrix}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & 0 \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a & c \\ 0 & d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a^2 & ac \\ ac & d^2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & -6 \\ -6 & 34 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Thus, $a^2 = 4$ and $d^2 = 34,$ so $a > 0$ and $d > 0.$ Also, $ac = -6,$ so $c = -3.$ Therefore, the matrix $\mathbf{L}$ is
\[\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ -3 & 6 \end{pmatrix}.\]
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ -3 & 6 \end{pmatrix}$.
