Problem:
Compute
\[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 & 0 \\ -7 & 4 & 2 \\ 0 & 5 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We perform the matrix multiplication as follows:
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 & 0 \\ -7 & -4 & 2 \\ 0 & 5 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -1 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot (-1) + 0 \cdot (-2) \\ -7 \cdot 4 + (-4) \cdot (-1) + 2 \cdot (-2) \\ 0 \cdot 4 + 5 \cdot (-1) + (-1) \cdot (-2) \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -24 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -4 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$.
