Problem:
Find the matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the $y$-axis.

Solution:
answer:  The matrix that corresponds to projecting onto the \( y \)-axis is the projection matrix onto the \( y \)-axis. This matrix is given by:

\[
\begin{pmatrix}
1 & 0 \\
0 & 1
\end{pmatrix}
\]

This matrix projects any vector onto the \( y \)-axis by setting the \( x \)-component to zero.
