Problem:
Let $\mathbf{v}$ and $\mathbf{w}$ be vectors such that
\[\text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -11 \end{pmatrix}.\]Find $\text{proj}_{-\mathbf{w}} (\mathbf{v})$.

Solution:
answer:  We know that $\text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w}$. Therefore, $\text{proj}_{-\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot (-\{w})}{(-\mathbf{w}) \cdot \mathbf{w}}(-\mathbf{w}) = -\frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\mathbf{w} \cdot \mathbf{w}} \mathbf{w} = -\text{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = -\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -11 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 11 \end{pmatrix}}$.
