answer:  We know that $\sin 3 \theta = \cos 7 \theta$ if and only if $3 \theta = 180^\circ - 7 \theta$ for some integer $k$. Simplifying, we get $10 \theta = 180^\circ$. Therefore, $\theta = \frac{180^\circ}{10} = 18^\circ$. The smallest positive angle $\theta$ that satisfies this equation is $\boxed{18^\circ}$.
