Problem:
Evaluate
\[\begin{vmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can expand the determinant along the first row:
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix} &= 0 \cdot \begin{vmatrix} 0 & c - b \\ b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix} - (b - a) \cdot \begin{vmatrix} a - b & c - b \\ a - c & 0 \end{vmatrix} + (c - a) \cdot \begin{vmatrix} a - b & 0 \\ a - c & b - c \end{vmatrix} \\
&= 0 - (b - a) \cdot (0 - (c - b)(a - c)) + (c - a) \cdot ((a - b)(b - c) - 0) \\
&= 0 - 0 + 0 \\
&= \boxed{0}.
\end{align*}
