Problem:
Find the reflection of $\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ over the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}.$

Solution:
answer:  The reflection of a point $\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix}$ over a vector $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}$ is given by the formula:

$$\begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}.$$

In this case, we have:

$$\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} - 2 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -6 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}}.$$
