Problem:
A plane contains the vector $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 2 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ and has normal vector $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 5 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}.$  A line contains the vector $\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}$ and has direction vector $\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ -1 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}.$  Find the point of intersection of the plane and line.

Solution:
answer:  The equation of the plane is $4x + 5y + 6z = 34.$  The equation of the line is $x = -1 - t,$ $y = -t,$ $ $z = 5 + 2t.$  Substituting into the equation of the plane, we get

$$4(-1 - t) + 5(-t) + 6(5 + 2t) = 34.$$Simplifying, we have

$$-4 - 4t - 5t + 30 + 12t = 34 \Rightarrow 3t = 6 \Rightarrow t = 2.$$Therefore, the point of intersection is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ -2 \\ 9 \end{pmatrix}}.$
