Problem:
Simplify
\[\frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression as

\[\frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\cos x}{1 - \sin x} - \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \boxed{0}.\]
