Problem:
Find $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 4 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}.$

Solution:
answer:  To add the vectors, we add their corresponding components:

\begin{align*}
\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 4 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 + 2 \\ 4 + (-1) \\ -6 + 3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}

