Problem:
For $\bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ -4 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix},$ compute $\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v}$.

Solution:
answer:  We have that $\text{proj}_{\bold{w}} \bold{v} = \frac{\bold{v} \cdot \bold{w}}{\bold{w} \cdot \bold{w}} \bold{w} = \frac{0(2) + (-4)(2) + 1(-1)}{2^2 + 2^2 + (-1)^2} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \frac{-9}{9} \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -\frac{2}{3} \\ -\frac{2}{3} \\ \frac{1}{3} \end{pmatrix}}.$
====================

