Problem:
If $\mathbf{A}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix},$ then find the inverse of $\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B}.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that $(\mathbf{A} \mathbf{B})^{-1} = \mathbf{A}^{-1} \mathbf{B}^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 0 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -1 & 3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 & 4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.$
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 8 & 4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}$. I hope it is correct.
