Problem:
Equilateral triangle $OAB$ has side length 1.  The point $P$ satisfies
\[\overrightarrow{OP} = (2 - t) \overrightarrow{OA} + t \overrightarrow{OB},\]where $t$ is a real number.  Find the minimum value of $|\overrightarrow{AP}|.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that
 $|\overrightarrow{AP}| = |\overrightarrow{OP} - \overrightarrow{OA}| = |(2 - t) \overrightarrow{OA} + t \overrightarrow{OB} - \overrightarrow{OA}| = |(1 - t) \overrightarrow{OA} + t \overrightarrow{OB}| = \sqrt{(1 - t)^2 + t^2} = \sqrt{1 - 2t + t^2} = \sqrt{(1 - t)^2} = |1 - t|.$

The minimum value of $|\overrightarrow{AP}|$ is $0$, which occurs when $t = 1$.
