Problem:
Simplify
\[\frac{\sin x}{\cos x} + \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression as

\[\frac{\sin x}{\cos x} + \frac{\cos x}{1 + \sin x} = \frac{\sin x (1 + \sin x)}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} + \frac{\cos x \cos x}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} = \frac{\sin x (1 + \sin x) + \cos x \cos x}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} = \frac{\sin x + \sin^2 x + \cos x}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} = \frac{\sin x + \cos x}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} = \frac{1}{\cos x (1 + \sin x)} = \frac{1}{\cos x + \cos x \sin x} = \frac{1}{\cos x + \sin^2 x} = \frac{1}{\cos x + \sin x} = \boxed{\frac{1}{\cos x + \sin x}}.\]
====================

