Problem:
Find all solutions to
\[\sin \left( \tan^{-1} (x) + \cot^{-1} \left( \frac{1}{x} \right) \right) = \frac{1}{3}.\]Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.

Solution:
answer:  We know that $\tan^{-1} (x) + \cot^{-1} \left( \frac{1}{x} \right) = \tan^{-1} (x) + \tan^{-1} \left( \frac{1}{x} \right) = \tan^{-1} \left( x \cdot \frac{1}{x} \right) = \tan^{-1} (1) = \frac{\pi}{4}$. Therefore, the equation becomes $\sin \left( \frac{\pi}{4} \right) = \frac{1}{3}$. This is not possible, so there are no solutions.
