Problem:
Simplify
\[\cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left (\frac {4 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{8 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac {16 \pi}{15} \right).\]

Solution:
answer:  We can use the property of cosine functions to simplify the expression. Notice that $\cos(2\theta) = \cos(\theta)$ for any angle $\theta$. Therefore, we can rewrite the expression as:

\[\cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{4 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{8 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{16 \pi}{15} \right) = \cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) \cos \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) = \cos^4 \left( \frac{2 \pi}{15} \right) = \boxed{1}.\]
