Solution:
answer:  The set \( S \) is the upper half of a sphere with radius 5 centered at the origin. The largest cube contained in this sphere will have its side length equal to the radius of the sphere. Therefore, the side length of the largest cube contained in \( S \) is \(\boxed{5}\).
