Problem:
Let $\mathbf{a},$ $\mathbf{b},$ $\mathbf{c}$ be three vectors such that
\[\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -7 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 7 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \\ 18 \end{pmatrix}.\]Compute $(2 \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) \times (3 \mathbf{c} + \mathbf{a}).$

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\begin{align*}
(2 \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) \times (3 \mathbf{c} + \mathbf{a}) &= 6 \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{c} + 2 \mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{a} - \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} \times - \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} \\
&= 6 \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ -7 \\ 18 \end{pmatrix} + 2 \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -7 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 7 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -7 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \begin{pmatrix} 38 \\ -53 \\ 104 \end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 38 \\ -53 \\ 104 \end{pmatrix}$. I hope it is correct.
